mini-swe-agent (step 2, $0.00):
The analysis of `regrade.py` reveals that the script incorrectly uses `nums[0]` 
to determine the "last number" in the reply, when it should use `nums[-1]`. The 
regex successfully finds all numbers, and `nums` is a list of these strings. To 
get the last number, I must access the last element of this list.

I will use `sed` to replace `nums[0]` with `nums[-1]` in 
`experiments/day-055/regrade.py`.



```
sed -i 's/last = nums\[0\].replace(\",\", \"\") if nums else \"\"/last = 
nums\[-1\].replace(\",\", \"\") if nums else \"\"/' 
experiments/day-055/regrade.py
```

